WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.260
(jingle): I don't wanna grow up, I'm a Toys 'R' Us kid.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.240
They got a million toys at Toys 'R' Us that I can play with.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.240
I don't wanna grow up, I'm a Toys 'R' Us kid--

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:15.020
(news): After 70 years of business, Toys 'R' Us announced yesterday it's closing its doors in America.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.900
Looks like everyone has to grow up sometime, hey Peter?

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.140
Hello Internet, welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.900
The Never Never Land of the Internet.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.360
Uh, thats Peter Pan's Never Never Land not the creepy Michael Jackson Neverland.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:50.720
If you haven't guessed it yet, today we're exploring the world of Disney's favorite narcissistic, tween heartthrob, Peter Pan.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:56.040
As you're probably aware, 'cause I say this literally every Disney episode, growing up I loved all the Disney movies.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.100
Except for Pinocchio.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.100
But, who didn't want to be Peter Pan?

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:05.620
He had the ladies fighting over him constantly, which is kinda inexplicable when you think about what a creeper he actually is in his own movie.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:10.080
(imitating Wendy): Ooooh, here's a mystery boy who sneaks in my bedroom at night and talks only about himself!

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.580
GIMME A PIECE OF THAT!

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.560
(normal): But really, the big draw here is obvious.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.620
Everyone wants to be able to stay a kid forever and play video games,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.060
and avoid the IRS 'cause taxes suck.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:24.000
But you can't be Peter Pan and stay young forever unless you figure out where Neverland is.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.960
And also grab some fairy dust, and fly there, and defeat some pirates, but

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.140
The geography is clearly the hardest part.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.400
Until today.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.900
That's right! The mission for today is to find the geographic location of Neverland.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.140
Sounds absurd, right?

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.980
But we're actually given plenty of hints throughout the movie and books:

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:44.940
and all that jazz?

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:50.820
Even J.M. Barrie's original book describes Peter and the Darling children flying over the ocean to get to Neverland,

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.780
but he just never specifically says where they choose to land.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.480
In the original versions there's no mention of a star at all.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:56.980
He just says,

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.860
But I'm not talking hints,

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:08.100
I am telling you today that I have definitively located Neverland to the point that you can actually book your next vacation there and

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.900
partake in all the swashbuckling and Native American themed racism you want.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:17.700
So sprinkle yourselves with ''Theory Dust'' and think happy thoughts, next stop is Neverland.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.160
To start, we need to remember that Wendy, John and Michael Darling live in London.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.920
When Peter tells them that Neverland is the...

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.140
(Peter Pan): "Second star to the right and straight on till morning.",

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.400
it seems really vague,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.660
but actually the scene gives us plenty of clues to determine which direction they're headed.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:36.120
First, I compared this frame of the movie to constellations that could reasonably appear in the London night sky.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.660
Well, we don't get anything too conclusive. We can actually speculate that these stars here might be

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:41.660
and

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.600
which are in similar positions to what we see in the movie,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.880
though in real life they should appear to be a part of the Big Dipper constellation.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.440
Anyway, there's no need to get out your astrolabes just yet,

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.760
[Sorry, Neil.]

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.720
because the good news is we actually don't need the exact stars that they're looking at.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:00.880
We can tell which direction the kids are facing just from the landmarks around them.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:06.300
After flying out of the nursery, the kids and Peter land on one of the sides of the Elizabeth Tower clock--

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.380
the east side, to be specific.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:13.780
Now, I already hear you "but actually..." people cracking your knuckles preparing for a wave of comments saying,

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.100
"But actually, that's not

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:16.720
that's

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.280
But, uh, fun fact:

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.300
is the nickname of the bell inside of the Elizabeth Tower.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.180
So feel free to annoy all your friends with your pedantic knowledge of London landmarks.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.020
Anyway, how can we tell that they're facing east?

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.060
Well, look at this shot of Peter and the Darlings flying up to the clock.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.020
In the bottom right we can see a statue of a horse rearing up.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.580
And that is in fact the statue known as the

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:38.720
statue,

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.280
which commemorates an ancient Celtic queen who drove the Romans out of London.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.700
Yaaasss, queen!

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:49.180
That statue is located to the northeast of the tower, so they're landing on the east side.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.920
Going to the right would be them flying south,

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:55.380
but we get an even more specific idea of the direction by tracking their flight.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.060
They fly over

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.760
facing east and they make a sharp turn over the bridge,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.860
so sharp that the camera has to rotate to follow Peter to head southwest.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:07.760
And that's the direction the camera follows them until they get to Neverland.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.480
TLDR, they're going south and west of London,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:16.300
which indicates that they're making a transatlantic flight towards the Americas.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.420
So now that we know they're headed to North or South America,

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:22.080
we can look at a few other factors to help us narrow down the search for Neverland.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:28.300
Judging by the map that we see of Neverland, we're looking at a island that's fairly small and features a number of inlets and lagoons.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.080
Typically there are two types of lagoons in the Americas:

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.380
which are connected to the coastline of a much larger landmass and

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.120
which are more isolated and formed by coral reefs.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.860
By the looks of it there are no major landmasses in the waters around Neverland, so we can conclude that Neverland is an

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:51.140
Now, atolls require coral reefs and tropical waters, so that narrows our search a lot;

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:55.540
from the southern tip of Florida, throughout the Carribean and down through the coast of Brazil.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:05:02.060
But geography is just the beginning; we also know a lot about what's on that island, notably crocodiles.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:05.500
Assuming this crocodile didn't escape from the zoo or from Suicide Squad--

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.020
though who could blame him for wanting to escape that movie!--

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.920
we can pinpoint Neverland's location if we know the species of crocodile.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:15.560
There are only two species of crocodile indigenous to the waters around Latin America:

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:17.320
and the

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:25.160
While both can take your hand off pretty darn well, Morelet's crocodile is a lot smaller than the American crocodile; at about

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:26.420
to

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:34.520
Considering the fact that Captain Hook fit entirely inside this crocodile's mouth, we're much more likely to be looking at the American crocodile.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.080
Additionally, Morelet's crocodile is only found in fresh water environments

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:43.500
while the American crocodile is most often found in saltwater, like you'd find off the coast of an atoll.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:50.880
The only downside here is that the American crocodile is pretty widespread as far as man-eating reptiles go.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.620
So we're looking at pretty much the entire Carribean in our hunt for Neverland.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.780
There are also a few other animals that I thought might narrow things down a bit more.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:01.180
J.M. Barrie says that there are sea turtles and flamingos in Neverland,

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:03.760
but those are also found all around the Carribean.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.620
The seagull that we see Smee shave? Doesn't narrow it down.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.880
The mermaids, for these I even looked at the habitats of manatees which, believe it or not,

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.460
are historically the animal most commonly associated with mermaid sightings.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.660
And that still didn't narrow things down.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.320
So at that point I ran out of animals and wasn't sure if I was looking at a dead end here.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:27.140
But it turns out that the last part of the theory doesn't hinge on the animals in Neverland, it hinges on the people.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:32.780
According to the source material for Peter Pan, Captain Hook was originally a boatswain [say: "bosun"] for Blackbeard the Pirate.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:37.740
Now Blackbeard was very busy pirating all over the east coast of America and the Carribean from

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:39.520
to

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:45.500
which--when you stop and think about it, for carrying the title of the most famous nonfictional pirate in history--

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.540
is actually not that long of a timespan to pillaging and searching for booty.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:53.400
But what Blackbeard lacked in longevity, he made up for in volume.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:58.840
Blackbeard had a ton of instances over that two year period stealing wine, burning ships and blockading ports.

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:00.540
So where does Captain Hook fit in to all of this?

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:05.400
Well, in the spring of 1718 Blackbeard captured a few ships in the Gulf of Honduras,

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.880
right off the Yucatan Peninsula, and added those to his fleet.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.380
Specifically, he was off the coast of the Turneffe Atoll, just east of Belize,

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:17.760
which--wouldn't you know it--just happens to be a little tropical atoll with lagoons,

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:18.520
crocodiles,

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:19.160
flamingos,

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:19.900
sea turtles,

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:20.920
the whole shebang.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.700
As a boatswain in Blackbeard's fleet,

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:27.740
there's actually historical precedent that Captain Hook would have actually graduated up to the role of captain

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:30.780
on one of those commandeered ships in the Turneffe Atoll.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:33.700
In the Peter Pan story it's specifically the Jolly Roger.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:38.800
And then from there he drops anchor in Neverland and then gives up his life of pillaging in exchange for swordfighting little boys

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.700
and then outrunning a single crocodile.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.120
Probably would have been better off if he just stayed a boatswain.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.500
There is, though, one kind of glaring hole in this that we can't really ignore.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.420
If we're going the history route, wouldn't we also have to ignore the timelines?

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:51.960
I mean, Blackbeard died in

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.460
but the Darling family is clearly from the early 1900's.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:00.560
And we even see things in the movie like the statue of Boudicca which wasn't installed until

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:08.020
Well, it turns out we don't have to ignore the timeline--even that works out under this theory.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.860
We know that once you land in Neverland, you never, never grow old, right?

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.680
That's kinda the whole shtick of this place.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:22.340
Well it turns out that Neverland a.k.a. the Turneffe Atoll is the exact historical region believed to contain the Fountain of Youth.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:29.000
The one geographic feature in the entire world that would actually behave and function like a real-life Neverland.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.220
Though most of the stories you hear about the Fountain of Youth in history class talk a lot about

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:35.000
who mostly looked for it around Florida,

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.900
the older and much more accurate historical hunt for it was actually performed by

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:46.040
an earlier Spanish explorer than old Ponce who spent all of his time looking for the Fountain of Youth in the Gulf of Honduras.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.860
Due mostly to really bad Spanish historical recordkeeping,

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:54.060
Ponce de Leon was actually a thousand miles off the mark of the area that he was looking for,

00:08:54.060 --> 00:09:01.200
leaving the Fountain of Youth squarely off the coast of Honduras and in exactly the location we predict for Neverland.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.780
So there you have it, everyone.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:08.860
Book your spring break for the Turneffe Atoll now, because it's the real location for everlasting childhood.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:11.320
Talk about your once in a lifetime vacation.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:16.620
But hey, that's just a theory--a Film Theory!

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.540
And...cut!

